// FIX BUILD (Gemini timeout + analytics counts + video parts) - what changed in this version
//  * #GmTimeoutFix: "Gemini Egress (Durable Object) problem: network error: timeout after 25 s". The Durable Object cut EVERY call at 25 s, but a
//    Gemini answer (StreamGenerate) can take longer (the log shows 11 s and 21 s runs). The caller now sends timeoutMs: StreamGenerate gets 85 s,
//    everything else keeps 25 s. A timeout no longer forces a second /app page-token fetch on the retry.
//  * #GmRotateFix: RotateCookies 429 bursts. gmRotate saved rotatedAt, but the token fetch / StreamGenerate paths then saved the OLD
//    store.rotatedAt back, so the 9-minute guard never held and every retry rotated again. rotatedAt is now kept on the shared store object,
//    and a 429 on rotation pauses rotation for 30 minutes.
//  * #VisitsFix (Admin > Live analytics, "Today" card): "visits" counted only video plays while "unique visitors" also counted browsers, so the
//    card showed 11 visits for 37 visitors (0.3 visits / visitor). A visit is now one visitor active in one hour (browsing OR playing), so
//    visits >= unique visitors. The hourly bars, peak hour, this hour, yesterday, vs yesterday, the 7 day strip and "Last 7 days" all use
//    the same definition. Video plays are shown on their own ("Video plays"); a live play event only raises that counter.
//  * #VideoParts: link the parts of a franchise (Spider-Man 2002 = Part 1, Spider-Man 2 2004 = Part 2, Spider-Man: Brand New Day 2026 = Part 3).
//    MANUAL (admin watch page > Parts) + AUTOMATIC: the AI checks title + release year of related videos the first time a video is opened,
//    the title alone groups them until then. Parts are ordered by release year and renumber themselves when a film is added.
//    Admin: Re-detect with AI, Scan whole library with AI, Automatic AI detection switch. Tables: video_parts, video_parts_checked.
//    The watch page shows a futuristic part timeline + previous / next part; the big player buttons, media keys and auto-next follow the parts.
// ============================================================================
// ============================================================================
// HUD + EGRESS GUARD BUILD - what changed in this version
//  * #AdminFree: the site protection script (right-click block, F12 / Ctrl+Shift+I / Ctrl+U / Ctrl+S block, devtools-open pause, video
//    drag / context-menu block) now skips itself for a VERIFIED admin session. The server (withAdminChrome) injects window.__tzAdmin = 1 at
//    the top of <head> only when the signed admin cookie is valid, so a normal visitor cannot unlock it by editing localStorage. Admin can
//    right-click, inspect, view-source and save the page everywhere on the site. Visitors are unchanged.
//  * #AnalyticsHUD: futuristic re-skin of the admin "Live analytics" panel (grid backdrop, glass stat cards with corner brackets, radar
//    "online now" card, neon table headers, value-change flash). Pure CSS + one tiny observer - no change to any data code or endpoint.
//  * #EgressGuard: one extra safety layer around every Facebook request and every Gemini request (details at the "#EgressGuard" block).
//    Switch: environment variable EGRESS_GUARD = "enforce" (default) | "monitor" (log only, never block) | "off".
//    Admin card: Live analytics -> "Egress Guard". Routes: GET/POST /api/admin/egress-guard.
//  * #AllCountries (bug fix): "Visitors by country" and "Unique visitors" only counted people who WATCHED a video (rows in video_views),
//    so every visitor who just browsed was missing and whole countries never showed. Each visitor is now recorded once per hour in a small
//    site_visitors table (one INSERT OR IGNORE per visitor-hour, same on/off switch as presence) and the today card merges both sources.
//    Also fixed: Cloudflare's special codes (T1 = Tor, XX = unknown) were cut down to a fake one-letter country; they are now "Unknown".
// ============================================================================
