// FUTURE SUITE BUILD - what changed in this version
//  * #ThemeSync: the splash, progress bar, PiP chip and ad-block wall now use the site theme colours (--primary / --secondary / --bg ...), and the
//    browser bar colour follows --bg - change the theme in admin and all of them follow.
//  * #Preloader: neon film-reel splash (spinning reel + site name + light sweep) on every full page load - 0.9 s on the first visit of a
//    session, 0.25 s after that, hard limit 3 s, no splash for crawlers or reduced-motion users. Soft navigation adds a short fade-up.
//  * #AdShield: layered ad-block protection (switch: FUTURE_SHIELD_MODE = "wall" | "warn" | "off").
//    - three independent checks: a bait element with ad class names, a bait script (/ads/adframe.js) and, when AdSense is on the page,
//      a request to the AdSense host. Two signals + a confirm pass are needed before the lock (no lock for a slow network or bots).
//    - the lock is a full-screen wall in a CLOSED shadow root with a random tag name (filter lists cannot target it), re-attached by a
//      MutationObserver + a 4 s guard, and HTMLMediaElement.play() is refused while it is up.
//    - ad-break integrity: while the site's own ad slate runs (#AdEngine) it is watched; hiding it, shrinking it or removing its creative
//      locks the player. Admin sessions, /admin, /login, /signup and crawlers are never locked.
//  * #PipEverywhere: Picture-in-Picture follows the viewer across the whole site. Clicking any in-site link while a video plays (or is
//    already in PiP) opens PiP first, then the next page is loaded WITHOUT a reload (soft navigation); the player stays alive, hidden,
//    so the PiP window is never cancelled. A small "Return / Stop" chip shows while it runs. PiP ends when the viewer closes it, opens
//    another video, taps Return (resumes at the same second via ?t=) or the video is about to end. Ad statistics are not counted while the
//    player runs in the background. Opt out per browser: localStorage.fb_pip_follow = "0". Chromium / Safari desktop (no iOS).
//  * #Preload: Speculation Rules prefetch (hover / touch) for Chromium, <link rel=prefetch> fallback elsewhere, idle warm-up of /series and /,
//    Data-Saver / 2G aware, never prefetches /watch (a prefetch of /watch is answered 204 so views and link resolving are not triggered).
//    Neon top progress bar on soft navigation.
//  * #Permalink / #SeoPlus: /watch?id=... is 301-redirected to /watch/<title>-<id>; every public page gets robots, canonical, Open Graph /
//    Twitter basics when missing, WebSite + SearchAction (home) and BreadcrumbList (watch) structured data; login / profile / search pages
//    are noindex.
