// ============================================================================
// GEMINI REDIRECT JAR BUILD - what changed in this version
//  * #GmRedirectJar: "Gemini Egress (Durable Object) problem: too many redirects" is fixed. gmFetchVia follows redirects itself through
//    the Durable Object; it now keeps a per-request cookie jar, so Set-Cookie headers sent on every redirect hop (consent, sign-in,
//    __Secure-1PSIDTS rotation) are applied to the next hop, exactly as a browser does. Before, the hop reused the saved cookies,
//    so a redirect that needed a cookie it had just been given looped until the 10-hop limit.
//  * Cookies set on intermediate hops are also handed back to the caller, so the saved login is kept fresh.
//  * #GmRedirectTrace: when a loop still happens, the error lists the host + path chain (no query strings, no cookie values),
//    e.g. "too many redirects (gemini.google.com/_/... > consent.google.com/m > gemini.google.com/...)".
// ============================================================================
// ORBIT SHIELD BUILD - what changed in this version
//  * #GmShield: an optional "device identity" layer on top of Gemini Egress (Orbit). While Orbit is FIXED or AUTO and the Shield is ON:
//      1) every Gemini request carries ONE pinned, internally consistent browser identity (user-agent + sec-ch-ua + platform + language),
//         chosen in Admin > AI > Gemini Egress > Orbit Shield (win-chrome is the default and equals the old DS_UA identity). A UA that
//         disagrees with its client hints is a classic bot tell; the profile keeps them matched.
//      2) proxy / edge headers that could reveal the Worker (x-forwarded-for, via, forwarded, true-client-ip, cf-*, cdn-loop ...) are
//         stripped twice: before the call (gmShieldApply) and again inside the Durable Object (defense in depth).
//      3) drift detection: each Durable Object hashes the identity it sends (fp, 8 hex chars) and counts a "drift" whenever it changes.
//         Admin "Scan" shows fp + drift per region; drift > 0 means some caller changed identity mid-session (Google sees a new device).
//  * Honest limits: the Cloudflare runtime decides the TLS / HTTP2 fingerprint and adds its own subrequest headers, so this layer cannot
//    change those. It keeps the identity STABLE and COHERENT; it does not make the Worker look like a real browser to Google.
//    Switching profile counts as a new device for the saved login, so pick one and keep it. Shield only runs while Orbit is ON.
//  * Settings in admin_prefs: gm_fp_shield = "1"|"0" (default off), gm_fp_profile = win-chrome | mac-chrome | linux-chrome. Cached 60 s with
//    the other Orbit settings. Routes: GET/POST /api/admin/gemini-egress now also carry { shield, profile }.
//
// GEMINI EGRESS "ORBIT" BUILD - what changed in this version
//  * #GmEgress (v2 "Orbit"): Gemini web-session traffic (public AI search, Add-video search / "Did you mean?" / auto-fill, description
//    writer, geminiSelfTest, #GmKeepAlive, cookie rotation) can leave from a Durable Object (class GeminiEgress, binding GEMINI_EGRESS)
//    created with a locationHint, so Google sees a stable Cloudflare region. Helper: gmFetch(env, url, init).
//  * THREE modes (Admin > AI > "Gemini Egress"): OFF = plain fetch (old behaviour, default) / FIXED = one region /
//    AUTO = a pool of up to 4 regions with health-aware failover: it stays "sticky" on the last good region, a failing region
//    is put on a growing cool-down (15 s, 30 s ... 120 s), and the next region in the pool takes over. There is NEVER a silent
//    fallback to a direct fetch (that would leak the real data-center IP); if every region fails you get a clear error.
//  * Live telemetry: each Durable Object counts requests / errors / average latency / last status. Admin "Scan" reads
//    https://www.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/trace through every active region (ip / colo / loc / ms) plus those counters.
//  * The Durable Object times out after 25 s and retries a failed GET once. It never stores or logs cookies or bodies.
//  * Routes: GET/POST /api/admin/gemini-egress, POST /api/admin/gemini-egress/check.
//    Settings live in admin_prefs (gm_do_mode = off|fixed|auto, gm_do_hint, gm_do_pool = "apac,eeur,weur"), cached 60 s.
//    The old gm_do_enabled = "1" is still understood (treated as FIXED) so an upgrade keeps working.
//
//  wrangler.toml - needs the binding and a NEW migration (the old class was deleted in v3, so it is re-created in v4):
//    [[durable_objects.bindings]]
//    name = "GEMINI_EGRESS"
//    class_name = "GeminiEgress"
//    [[migrations]]
//    tag = "v4"
//    new_sqlite_classes = ["GeminiEgress"]
// ============================================================================
